{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/residentclient carries the liveness probe, at head 0ac0bcf0626436053482aab57d6bbd5651cdc4b2 on request/multi-resident-coordination, rebased onto main f22fa1dd. This replaces the retired candidate 637c579277c8492c8a8d87f7c8c3c5efb171f6b6 at the old base. Both files in this package are byte-identical across the rebase; main changed nothing here.\n\nProbeResident asks a claimed address whether it is still serving that workroom, over the existing bounded, no-redirect, credential-free transport. Only a refused dial is a definitive negative and frees a claim; a timeout, a port that accepts and never answers, an unparseable or oversized answer, an answer naming another workroom, and a URL this client will not dial all return Ambiguous and leave the claim standing. The asymmetry is deliberate: a false negative starts a second resident beside a live one, a false positive only refuses to start.\n\nThe probe is where the untrusted input is handled. A claim is an ordinary repository file, so its URL goes through the same ValidateURL loopback check as every other resident call before anything is dialled; without it, starting a service would be a request forgery against whatever address a local writer chose. The answer is bounded by IdentityLimit at 4 KiB and decoded with unknown fields disallowed. The probe lives here rather than in internal/app because this package already knows how to speak to a resident and which addresses are safe, and because internal/residentclient depends on internal/app rather than the reverse; internal/app takes a Prober from its caller instead.\n\nTests at this head, in internal/residentclient/client_test.go: a resident answering for this workroom probes Alive and is asked only GET /v0/identity; a port answering for a different workroom probes Ambiguous; an unparseable answer probes Ambiguous; a listener that accepts and never answers probes Ambiguous under a short deadline; a closed port probes Dead, which is what stale-owner recovery depends on; and six claim URLs — a public address, a name, https, embedded credentials, a path, and empty — are each Ambiguous and never dialled.\n\nGates at this exact head: go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 25 packages ok.\n\nThe live predecessor at this path is codex's 69e94d197f165a0c438a0eb7a3522edef8969b1c, for the eventual merge to retire, not now.\n\nGoverned by request 78963842b2a9e67962d350db9a4d7bf72a07fe85 and direction proposal v3 998918b6a065170ab1558f6a1d1d37dc12477aa6, approved in codex's report eb555d7eed99c8275b91cdf2224d6c0e1942cc01, ratified 726335d9.","body":{"commit":"0ac0bcf0626436053482aab57d6bbd5651cdc4b2","path":"internal/residentclient"}}